Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: parser.c
Line: 7755
Function: xmlLoadEntityContent
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The code checks for a leading '<?xml' using CMP5(CUR_PTR, ...) and IS_BLANK_CH(NXT(5)) without first ensuring that at least 6 bytes are available in the input buffer (no prior GROW). For short external entity contents, these macros can read past the end of the buffer, causing an out-of-bounds read. This is attacker-triggerable via an external parsed entity with very short content.

